From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:09:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Give IOMMU1 the 2D accelerator
 port gate

A master's register block in the IOMMU does not answer while the
master's port on the MBUS matrix is gated, and the access stalls the
bus. The IOMMU driver takes a reference on the port gate of a master,
given as a "masterN" clock, for as long as the master translates. The
A733 clock driver marks these gates CLK_IS_CRITICAL, so they stay
enabled and the reference does not change their state.

Name the port gate of the 2D accelerator, master 4 of the second IOMMU
(manual chapter 10). It is in the display engine system (DE_SYS) and
uses the same MBUS port as the display engine, DESYS, bit 11 of
MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG (manual section 4.1.6.83).

Nothing changes until a node lists the IOMMU in "iommus": the driver
enables a master clock only for a master with a user.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the 2D accelerator enabled for a test,
IOMMU1 holds the DE_SYS port gate for master 4 from boot on, one enable
more than with the node disabled.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 0c0e96a99043..8ee1ba658c5e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1127,9 +1127,10 @@ iommu1: iommu@3910000 {
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_DESYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_DESYS>;
 			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
-				      "master0", "master1", "master2";
+				      "master0", "master1", "master2", "master4";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU1_SYS>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
